<title>USA: US rep Kennedy says heatoil initiative falls short.</title>
<headline>US rep Kennedy says heatoil initiative falls short.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Congressman Joseph P. Kennedy (Democrat, Massachusetts) said Friday that Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary's meeting with oil company executives had produced nothing to shield consumers from heating oil price spikes this winter.</p>
<p>&quot;Although I am encouraged that the Department of Energy is looking at ways to make sure we do not have this problem in the future, this will do nothing to ensure that the consumers in the northeast are not left out in the cold this winter,&quot; Kennedy said in a statement.</p>
</text>
